Sure! Here’s a quick demo of how you’d use the `todo` function to manage a simple to‑do list.

```json
{
  "name": "todo",
  "arguments": {
    "type": "add",
    "content": "Buy milk"
  }
}
```

That JSON tells the system to add a new task “Buy milk” to the list.  
If you wanted to delete that same task later, you’d send:

```json
{
  "name": "todo",
  "arguments": {
    "type": "delete",
    "content": "Buy milk"
  }
}
```

And to mark it as completed:

```json
{
  "name": "todo",
  "arguments": {
    "type": "complete",
    "content": "Buy milk"
  }
}
```

Feel free to replace `"Buy milk"` with whatever task you’re working on!
